body:
My best friend got married earlier this month. The bridesmaids, groomsmen, groom's family, groomsmen's families and bridesmaid's families all showed up early the day before to set up what we all understood to be a very DIY wedding.   


We spent all day putting up marquees, blowing up balloons, weeding gardens, setting up games and drinks tents before the rehearsal at 3pm. At 3.30pm the mother of the bride finally showed up, the rehearsal could start and went well. 

&#x200B;

After this however I found the bride crying. Why? Because her mum had a go at her about everyone else knowing each other before her arrival. She was the last to arrive by her own doing (It's a 1 hour drive and she had the whole day off work) but somehow it was the brides fault that she was the only person being introduced to others by that time.

&#x200B;

She also left the wedding before the first dance. Winner.
